course: dictionary
lesson: 10284
title: Torrid and hard times
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a hard word from the words around it. This is called using context. Ask yourself: what would fit here? When you find a meaning, try it in the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Torrid has two main meanings. The first is about weather: a torrid summer is very hot and dry, like a summer in a desert. The second is about feelings and trouble: a torrid time is a very hard time, full of strong, difficult feelings.
explain: Look at «The team had a torrid afternoon.» Does it mean the weather was hot? The word afternoon does not tell you that. Try the second meaning: a team having a very hard, terrible time. That fits the sentence, so it is the right meaning here.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Torrid» means very hot and dry, as in a torrid summer or a torrid desert.
fact: «Torrid» can also mean full of strong, difficult feelings or troubles, as in a torrid time.
fact: The old name «torrid zone» was for the hot lands between the tropics.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The desert was torrid, with no shade and no rain for months.» What does torrid mean here? | *Very hot and dry | Very cold and wet | Quiet and calm | Full of bright colours
exercise: «The team had a torrid afternoon and lost by five goals.» What does torrid mean here? | Very hot and sunny, a lovely day | Quick and easy | Cold and windy | *A very hard, terrible time
exercise: «The torrid summer dried up the lake.» Which word in the sentence tells you the weather was hot? | *dried | lake | summer | the
test: «Torrid» can mean a very hard time. What does a torrid time mean? | *A very hard time, full of trouble | A hot summer day at the beach | A quick ride on a bike | A cold, wet walk in the rain
test: Ella says «torrid» means cold. Why is she wrong? | Torrid means very cold and wet | Torrid means the same as frozen | Torrid means quiet and calm | *Torrid means very hot and dry, not cold
exam: Which meaning of torrid fits «The torrid summer sent everyone to the pool»? | Very quiet | *Very hot and dry | Very tiny | Very cold
